# Cloudflare Pages redirects for mion.io.
#
# 2026-09: the site became ONE site with three subsites. Every page that used to
# live at the root of the site moved under /rpc, and the mion server
# benchmarks under /benchmarks/rpc. The first matching rule wins, so a page renamed
# after its move gets its own rule above the section splat (one hop, never a chain).
# Redirects apply BEFORE static files, so the
# benchmark pages are listed one by one: a `/benchmarks/*` splat would loop on the
# new /benchmarks/... paths.
/introduction/about-mion      /rpc  301
/introduction/about-mion-rpc  /rpc  301
/introduction/*  /rpc/introduction/:splat  301
/server/middle-fns  /rpc/server/middleware  301
/server/*        /rpc/server/:splat        301
/drizzle-orm/indexes-constraints  /rpc/drizzle-orm/constraints  301
/drizzle-orm/*   /rpc/drizzle-orm/:splat   301
/client/*        /rpc/client/:splat        301
/devtools/eslint-rules  /rpc/devtools/linter  301
/devtools/vite-config   /rpc/devtools/vite    301
/devtools/pure-functions  /runtypes/guide/pure-functions  301
/devtools/*      /rpc/devtools/:splat      301
/platforms/*     /rpc/platforms/:splat     301
# Binary serialization was removed (2026-09): its guide, the articles section and the formats benchmark.
# The JSON serialization page then merged into the serialization page.
/articles/*           /runtypes/guide/json-round-trip  301
/rpc/articles/*       /runtypes/guide/json-round-trip  301
/runtypes/articles/*  /runtypes/guide/json-round-trip  301
/runtypes/guide/binary-serialization         /runtypes/guide/json-round-trip       301
/runtypes/guide/json-serialization           /runtypes/guide/json-round-trip       301
/benchmarks/runtypes/serialization-formats  /benchmarks/runtypes/json-round-trip  301
# Each subsite home moved to its subsite root (2026-10): /runtypes is the page itself, so
# its old long address redirects to it. Every rule lands on its final page in one hop.
/rpc/introduction/about-mion-rpc            /rpc         301
/runtypes/introduction/about-mion-runtypes  /runtypes    301
/benchmarks/introduction/mion-benchmarks    /benchmarks  301
# Renamed (2026-09): a page whose file name contains "index" is mistaken for a folder
# index by Nuxt Content's navigation builder (an unanchored /index/ match) and nests
# under itself in the sidebar, so the slug lost the word.
/rpc/drizzle-orm/indexes-constraints  /rpc/drizzle-orm/constraints  301
# The about pages were rewritten as the subsite homes (2026-09) under new names.
/rpc/introduction/about-mion              /rpc       301
/runtypes/introduction/about-ts-runtypes  /runtypes  301
# The RunTypes section collapsed from three pages into one when the two docs
# sites merged (2026-08-24), and that page went too (2026-09): RunTypes has its own
# subsite, so every old RunTypes path lands on its home page.
/run-types       /runtypes  301
/run-types/*     /runtypes  301
/rpc/run-types   /runtypes  301
# The diagnostics page split into a section (2026-09): the levels page keeps the old
# address's readers, the code list is its second page.
/runtypes/diagnostics  /runtypes/diagnostics/error-levels  301
/benchmarks/hello-world       /benchmarks/rpc/hello-world       301
/benchmarks/light-validation  /benchmarks/rpc/light-validation  301
/benchmarks/heavy-validation  /benchmarks/rpc/heavy-validation  301
/benchmarks/payload-sizes     /benchmarks/rpc/payload-sizes     301
# The compile-time page kept only its type-checking half and was renamed for it, and
# the correctness page is parked (container/website/parked/) until its audit lane runs
# on deploy again; its nearest live page is the is-valid one.
/benchmarks/runtypes/compiletime   /benchmarks/runtypes/type-checking  301
/benchmarks/runtypes/correctness   /benchmarks/runtypes/is-valid       301
# middleFns were renamed to middleware (2026-09).
/rpc/server/middle-fns  /rpc/server/middleware  301
# The RunTypes guide split into sections (2026-09): Type Formats became its own
# section with a page per family, and linting plus source conversion moved to Tooling.
/runtypes/guide/type-formats              /runtypes/type-formats/overview      301
/runtypes/guide/decoding-untrusted-input  /runtypes/guide/json-round-trip        301
/runtypes/guide/json-schema-generation    /runtypes/guide/json-schemas         301
/runtypes/guide/linting                   /runtypes/tooling/linting            301
/runtypes/guide/source-conversion         /runtypes/tooling/source-conversion  301
# Each middleware's client page merged into its page, as a Client tab (2026-10).
/rpc/middlewares/fetch-metadata-client  /rpc/middlewares/fetch-metadata  301
/rpc/middlewares/sync-routes-client     /rpc/middlewares/sync-routes     301
